<div class="prose about" id="person">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>Practical engineering.<br>Long-term thinking.</h1>
  <p class="lead">I’m a software engineer focused on enterprise .NET applications: understanding how they work, keeping them reliable, and making them easier to change.</p>
  <p>I enjoy the investigative side of the work. When documentation is incomplete, I use the code and the system’s behavior to build an understanding of what’s happening and why.</p>
  <section class="ruled-section">
    <h2>Development, with a support perspective</h2>
    <p>I joined RevSpring in 2018 as a .NET developer. After moving into product support, I returned to development in 2022. That experience gave me a practical view of how enterprise software behaves in production and what it takes to keep it working.</p>
    <p>My work has included workflow orchestration and document-processing applications, spanning C# services, Angular interfaces, SQL Server, and integrations with older systems.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="ruled-section">
    <h2>Understanding a system, then owning the work</h2>
    <p>During two years embedded with an external development team, I became an internal subject-matter expert on a complex enterprise application. My responsibilities have included feature development, single sign-on fixes, production troubleshooting, and hotfix delivery.</p>
    <p>I’m most interested in hands-on work: tracing a problem across layers, making a focused change, and following it through to a working result.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="ruled-section">
    <h2>Tools I work with</h2>
    <p>C# and .NET, ASP.NET, Angular and TypeScript, and SQL Server form the core of my application work. I also work with Git, Azure DevOps, Windows, and Linux.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="ruled-section">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>I earned a B.S. in Information Technology from the University of Central Florida in 2017. Earlier experience included more than a year as a NASA intern working with HR information systems and workforce planning.</p>
    <p class="muted">Here, I write about software, Linux, and developer tools, with an emphasis on the details that make a solution reproducible.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="ruled-section">
    <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>
    <p>You can find my code on <a href="{{ site.github }}" rel="me">GitHub</a>, or connect with me on <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" rel="me">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
